add('G01','P2','Delivery','Checks are useful but do not cover the strongest product guarantees',
'All 10 spec gates and 42 backend tests pass, yet the added probes reproduce arithmetic, comparison, cache and version-gate defects. There is no committed CI configuration or frontend test suite in these two repositories, and the spec repo has no pinned Python dependency manifest.',
'Local green checks can be mistaken for broad conformance. Dependency/environment drift and new IR fields can silently weaken validation.',
'Add CI for the existing gates, backend tests, typecheck, production build and audit; pin Python dependencies. Convert the review probes into expected-correctness regression tests after fixes. Add generated numeric/layout vectors and a small end-to-end author→publish→run→compare flow.',
'Clean checkout builds against a pinned engine; fail CI on semantic regression and changed/uncovered IR fields.',[(ROOT,'tools/run_gates.py','There is no CI here'),(SAAS,'frontend/package.json','"scripts"')],'Repository inventory + executed checks')

def refs_html(refs):
    blocks=[]
    for root,rel,needle in refs:
        p=root/rel
        lines=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines()
        index=next((i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if needle in l),None)
        if index is None: raise RuntimeError((rel,needle))
        label=f'{root.name}/{rel}:{index+1}'
        snippet='\n'.join(f'{i+1:>4}  {lines[i]}' for i in range(max(0,index-1),min(len(lines),index+4)))
        blocks.append(f'<details><summary>{e(label)}</summary><pre>{e(snippet)}</pre></details>')
    return ''.join(blocks)

